-- Nakama demo data. NOT part of the migrations: run it by hand when you want a small database to try the app on.
--
-- Deliberately minimal, so that whatever shows up in Analytics is what you do yourself:
--   * 5 users: the two login accounts (admin@nakama.com, administrator; user@nakama.com) and 3 team members.
--   * 2 chatbots: "Soporte de Ingenieria" (active) and "Guia de Onboarding" (draft), with their team and no documents.
--   * 2 formations: "Bienvenida al equipo" (active, 2 modules, one of them a quiz) and "Seguridad basica" (draft).
--   * The Anthropic provider with the Claude model catalog, disabled and WITHOUT an API key: paste yours in the
--     "Proveedores de IA" screen and enable it.
--   * No conversations, no feedback and no user activity: Analytics starts at zero.
--
-- Accounts: admin@nakama.com and user@nakama.com, both with password Admin123.
-- The members live under @seed.nakama.test and use the password Seed1234.
--
-- Usage, once the API has applied the migrations:
--   docker exec -i nakama-postgres psql -U nakama -d nakama < docs/db/demo-data.sql
--
-- It can be run more than once: rows that already exist are skipped.

BEGIN;

SET client_encoding = 'UTF8';
SET standard_conforming_strings = on;


COMMIT;
